Third-party data in t/data
==========================

standard_1020_subset.elc
------------------------
28 positions (LPA, RPA, Nz, the 19 standard 10-20 electrodes, Fpz, Oz,
M1, M2, A1, A2) extracted without modification from

    fieldtrip/template/electrode/standard_1020.elc
    https://github.com/fieldtrip/fieldtrip
    commit 0b62f10a09dc589e5262992f341614a6737f0805 (2011-05-10)

The coordinate values are identical to those in that file, which is also
the file shipped with MNE-Python as
mne/channels/data/montages/standard_1020.elc.

Copyright Robert Oostenveld and the FieldTrip contributors.
Licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later.

The electrode positions are defined in:
    Oostenveld R, Praamstra P (2001) The five percent electrode system
    for high-resolution EEG and ERP measurements.
    Clinical Neurophysiology 112:713-719.

standard_1020_eog_nose.elc
--------------------------
37 positions from three sources:

  - The 19 standard 10-20 electrodes (T3/T4/T5/T6 naming) and the three
    fiducials LPA, RPA, Nz: the New York Head electrode coordinates
    (sa/locs_3D_orig), in MNI mm. All 22 are identical to the values
    dumped by examples/dump_nyhead19.pl.
    Iz, Fpz and Oz are in the same coordinate style and their labels are
    in the New York Head channel list, but they are not in that dump and
    have not been checked against it directly.

    The New York Head:
        https://www.parralab.org/nyhead/
    Copyright (C) 2015 Yu Huang, Lucas C. Parra and Stefan Haufe.
    Licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later.
        Huang Y, Parra LC, Haufe S (2016) The New York Head - a precise
        standardized volume conductor model for EEG source localization
        and tES targeting. NeuroImage 140:150-162.

  - M1, M2, A1, A2: from the FieldTrip file cited above, unmodified.

  - X1, hEOG, lhEOG, lvEOG, rhEOG, rvEOG, vEOG and nose: coordinates
    chosen by the author on the New York Head scalp mesh.

